cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "FloralPro: la flor, verticilo por verticilo — a browser-based app for teaching floral structure, floral formulas and floral diagrams"
abstract: >-
  FloralPro is a self-contained web application for teaching the structure of the flower,
  entirely in the browser, with no installation and no server. A single whorl-by-whorl model
  of each flower is drawn as a floral formula in the classic and Prenner conventions, a floral
  diagram, a rotatable 3D flower and a labelled longitudinal section, all linked. It includes
  a flower builder with botanical consistency checks, an atlas of 115 variant plates with a
  glossary, 82 angiosperm families arranged according to APG IV with 278 species and their
  status in Mexico, a multi-access and a generated dichotomous key, self-assessment with
  piece-by-piece grading and verifiable teacher exams, gymnosperm strobili in 3D as a contrast
  with the flower, and a classroom mode to project presentations and print sheets, worksheets
  and study cards. The interface is in Spanish and English.
